# Store credentials — Google's half
#
# Apple's .p8/.p12/.jks are covered above. The Play service account JSON was
# not, and it is the credential that arrives *after* Play approves you, which
# is exactly when it gets dropped in the repo root to fill in eas.json. This
# repository is public. A committed key is a compromised key even if the
# commit is reverted, because it was served to anyone watching in between.
*service-account*.json
google-play-*.json
play-store-*.json

# Where eas.json expects the Play key. Tracked README, ignored contents.
/certs/*
!/certs/README.md
